::id(doc-manifestDocRf)

=[ Manifest Reference ]

Generated by `catasto spec manifest` from Rust schema definitions in `crates/catasto-manifest/`. Do not edit it: change the doc comments there and run the command again.

Authoritative reference of all declarations and fields supported in `catasto.ctmt`.

==[ upstream ]

Upstream repository definitions declared in `::upstream(...)`. An upstream declares a named `catasto.git(...)` repository at a pinned revision, optionally with a `path` directory inside the repository from which entry paths start.

- `url` (string): Repository URL (`https://` URL or workspace-relative path), passed to `catasto.git(...)`.
- `rev` (string, default: `main`): Pinned tag, branch, or commit hash. Quote numeric revisions (e.g. `rev: "1.2"`).
- `path` (path): Directory or file inside the upstream repository that entry paths are relative to.

==[ zone ]

Directory schema rules declared in `::zone(...)`. A zone maps a workspace-relative directory path pattern (using `<?...>` holes, or `"."` for the workspace root) to constraints on child entries of each matching directory (and, when `recursive: true`, its non-ignored subdirectories).

- `require` (pattern | (pattern, ...)): Entry patterns that must each be matched by at least one non-ignored child entry.
- `allow` (pattern | (pattern, ...)): Entry patterns forming an allowlist; when present, every non-ignored child entry must match at least one.
- `deny` (pattern | (pattern, ...)): Entry patterns that no non-ignored child entry may match.
- `ignore` (pattern | (pattern, ...)): Entry patterns excluded from `require`, `allow`, `deny`, and recursive traversal.
- `recursive` (boolean, default: `false`): Whether this zone recursively applies to non-ignored subdirectories.
- `files` ((require: ..., allow: ..., deny: ...)): Nested constraints (`require`, `allow`, `deny`) applied only to non-directory entries.
- `dirs` ((require: ..., allow: ..., deny: ...)): Nested constraints (`require`, `allow`, `deny`) applied only to directory entries.

==[ entry ]

Manifest entry declaring a managed workspace file, directory, or submodule. Each top-level entry in `catasto.ctmt` binds a workspace-relative path to a `catasto.{upstream,git,local}(...)` constructor call, or a tuple `(call, executable: bool, symlink: follow | keep, submodule: bool)` pairing the source with placement options.

- `source` (catasto.upstream(...) | catasto.git(...) | catasto.local(...)): Constructor call declaring where canonical content comes from: `catasto.upstream(name, path: "...")`, `catasto.git(url, rev: ..., path: "...")`, or `catasto.local("...")`.
- `executable` (boolean): Whether a managed file is placed executable (`true`) or not (`false`), whatever the source says. Left out, the source decides: a git file's `100755` or not, and a local file is never executable. Rejected when `submodule: true`.
- `symlink` (follow | keep, default: `follow`): How symlinks in a git or upstream source are handled (`follow` or `keep`). Rejected on `catasto.local` or when `submodule: true`.
- `submodule` (boolean, default: `false`): Whether to clone a git or upstream source as a Git submodule and register it in `.gitmodules`. Rejected on `catasto.local`.
